  "title": "Introducing Ren, the AI anime maker that directs every shot",
  "link": "https://picsart.com/blog/introducing-ai-anime-maker-agent/",
  "pub_date": "Thu, 29 Oct 2026 13:47:09 +0000",
  "author": "Julia Tovmasyan",
  "content_snippet": "Ren is an AI anime maker on Picsart that turns a story idea, a photo or a video clip of your own into original anime. Ren works as your anime director, handling the cast, the shot list and the final edit. The results come in three sizes: vertical clips for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube … \nContinue reading \"Introducing Ren, the AI anime maker that directs every shot\"",
  "content_full": "<p><strong>Ren is an AI anime maker on Picsart that turns a story idea, a photo or a video clip of your own into original anime.</strong> <a href=\"https://picsart.com/ai-agents/ren-anime-studio/\">Ren</a> works as your anime director, handling the cast, the shot list and the final edit. The results come in three sizes: vertical clips for TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts, full episodes, and series where every character keeps the same look from one episode to the next. Here is what Ren is, what sets it apart and what you can make with it.</p>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-video\" style=\"max-width: 100%; margin: 28px auto;\"><video style=\"width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 1920 / 1080; border-radius: 12px;\" title=\"Ren AI anime maker demo turning a pet rooster into an anime fighter battling crows\" src=\"https://cdnblog.picsart.com/2026/10/ren-ai-anime-maker-demo.mp4\" controls=\"controls\" width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" aria-label=\"Ren AI anime maker demo turning a pet rooster into an anime fighter battling crows\" autoplay loop muted playsinline preload=\"auto\"></video></figure>\n<h2><span id=\"What_is_Ren\">What is Ren?</span></h2>\n<p>Ren is an AI agent built to direct anime. It covers four jobs in one place:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Writing:</strong> a script and a shot list for every episode.</li>\n<li><strong>Character design:</strong> a full turnaround sheet for each character.</li>\n<li><strong>Direction:</strong> one thing in every shot that the eye cannot miss, with cuts timed to the beat.</li>\n<li><strong>Quality control:</strong> Ren reviews every take first and redoes just the takes that fall short.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The idea behind it is that timing matters more than motion in anime. Even a motionless sky can hold a scene when the edit hits the beat, and Ren builds every clip around that rule.</p>\n<h2><span id=\"What_makes_Ren_different_a_cast_that_stays_on_model\">What makes Ren different: a cast that stays on model</span></h2>\n<p>Each character Ren creates gets a full turnaround sheet. Once you lock a character, each face, hairstyle and outfit stays consistent across shots and across episodes.</p>\n<p>Two more promises come with every project:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Original looks only.</strong> Ask for a mood or a genre and Ren creates a look in that spirit. It won&#8217;t reproduce a well-known series or its characters.</li>\n<li><strong>Price first.</strong> The credit price appears before anything renders, and a low-cost preview arrives before every final.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><span id=\"Who_is_Ren_for\">Who is Ren for?</span></h2>\n<p>Ren suits anyone who wants anime without drawing or animating it by hand. Four groups get the most out of it:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Social creators</strong> who need short vertical anime clips for TikTok, Reels and Shorts.</li>\n<li><strong>Storytellers</strong> who want full episodes, or a series with a cast that holds across episodes.</li>\n<li><strong>Brands</strong> that want their own product clips restyled as anime.</li>\n<li><strong>Fans of the style</strong> who want to see their own photo turned into an anime character.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2><span id=\"What_you_can_make_with_Ren\">What you can make with Ren</span></h2>\n<p>Ren&#8217;s range runs from five-second clips up to multi-episode series. Here are six things to make with it.</p>\n<h3>A vertical hook for your feed</h3>\n<p>Social clips run 5 to 30 seconds, framed vertically for TikTok, Reels and Shorts. Openings, fight beats and character moments all fit the format, each built around an impact frame that lands on the beat.</p>\n<h3>An episode for the big screen</h3>\n<p>An episode starts as a script, becomes a shot list and ends as an edited cut, and Ren shows you each stage before the next one begins. The result can be a cold open with two rivals that plays like a real show.</p>\n<h3>An anime version of yourself</h3>\n<p>Your own photo becomes an anime character with its own character sheet. Ren then animates that character in a shot that keeps your likeness.</p>\n<h3>A scene built from a mood</h3>\n<p>Describe the feeling you love rather than a show you love. Ren designs an original look in that spirit, so the result belongs to you.</p>\n<h3>Your product, restyled as anime</h3>\n<p>Ren can turn a clip you shot into anime, keeping the original movement and pacing intact. That includes product clips, which move the same way they did on camera.</p>\n<h3>A recurring cast</h3>\n<p>Once the characters are locked, later shots and episodes reuse the same faces, which is what makes a recurring series possible.</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Clips_episodes_or_series_which_one_to_make\">Clips, episodes or series: which one to make</span></h2>\n<p>Each format answers a different goal. Use this table to pick a starting point.</p>\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\">\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; table-layout: auto;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #000000; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap;\">Format</th>\n<th style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #000000; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap;\">What you get</th>\n<th style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #000000; font-weight: bold; white-space: nowrap;\">Best for</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Social clip</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">A vertical piece of 5 to 30 seconds, built around one impact frame</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Openings, fight beats and character moments for the feed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Episode</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">A written script, a shot list and the edited cut, each shown to you in turn</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">A standalone story such as a cold open with two rivals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Series</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Several episodes with locked characters and matching turnaround sheets</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #333333; padding: 10px 14px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; color: #ffffff; background: #141414;\">Recurring stories where the cast has to look the same every time</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</figure>\n<p>A clip is the fastest way to test a look. An episode adds a script and structure. A series builds on both, since its characters carry over from one episode to the next.</p>\n<h2><span id=\"How_to_make_your_own_anime_with_Ren\">How to make your own anime with Ren</span></h2>\n<p>Getting started takes four steps, for one clip or a whole series.</p>\n<h3>Step 1. Open Ren</h3>\n<p>Go to <a href=\"https://picsart.com/ai-agents/ren-anime-studio/\">Ren&#8217;s page</a> and click <strong>Open Ren</strong>.</p>\n<h3>Step 2. Add your starting point</h3>\n<p>Start from whichever you have. An idea works for a new story, a photo works for an anime version of yourself, and a clip works for restyling your own footage.</p>\n<h3>Step 3. Review each stage</h3>\n<p>For an episode, check the script, then the shot list, then the edited cut. Lock the characters once their turnaround sheets look right.</p>\n<h3>Step 4. Check the price and the preview</h3>\n<p>See the credit price before the render runs, watch the low-cost preview, then go to the final.</p>\n<p><section class=\"tips_block\" data-pulse-section-group=\"blog article\">\n    <h3 class=\"tips_title\">Tips for better anime with Ren</h3>\n\n    <div class=\"tips_list\" data-pulse-section=\"blog article_tips\">\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Name a feeling, not a franchise</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">Ren designs original looks, so a mood or a genre gives it more to work with than the title of a show.</p>\n            </article>\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Lock characters early</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">Turnaround sheets are what keep faces and outfits steady, so settle them before a series grows.</p>\n            </article>\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Use the preview</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">The low-cost preview shows pacing and framing problems before the final render spends credits.</p>\n            </article>\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Think in beats</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">Social clips work best around one impact frame that lands on the beat.</p>\n            </article>\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Start from your own footage for real motion</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">Restyled clips keep their original movement and pacing, which suits any shot where the real motion matters.</p>\n            </article>\n                    <article class=\"tips_item\">\n                <div class=\"tips_item_header\">\n                    <span class=\"tips_item_icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n                    <h4 class=\"tips_item_title\">Check each stage of an episode</h4>\n                </div>\n                <p class=\"tips_item_body\">Reviewing the script and the shot list early saves changes later in the edit.</p>\n            </article>\n            </div>\n</section>\n<br />\n<section class=\"section_faq\" id=\"faq-faq-6ae3567ec3c5a\">\n            <h2 class=\"faq_title\" id=\"Get_answers_to_common_questions\">Get answers to common questions</h2>\n    \n    <div class=\"faq_items\">\n                    <div class=\"faq_item faq_item--active\">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"true\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">What is Ren on Picsart?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"false\">\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>Ren is an AI anime maker built as an agent on Picsart. It makes original anime clips, episodes and series from your ideas, photos or footage.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n                    <div class=\"faq_item \">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">What can you bring to Ren?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-collapsed>\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>A story idea, a photo or a video clip. Each one leads to a different kind of result, from a new story to an anime version of yourself to restyled footage.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n                    <div class=\"faq_item \">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">How long are Ren&#039;s social clips?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-collapsed>\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>Social clips run from 5 to 30 seconds, in vertical format for TikTok, Reels and Shorts.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n                    <div class=\"faq_item \">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">Can you turn a photo of yourself into an anime character?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-collapsed>\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>Yes. Ren turns the photo into a character sheet first, then into a moving shot that keeps your likeness.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n                    <div class=\"faq_item \">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">How do characters stay consistent across episodes?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-collapsed>\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>Each character gets a full turnaround sheet. Once locked, faces, hair and outfits hold in every later shot and episode.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n                    <div class=\"faq_item \">\n                <button type=\"button\" class=\"faq_question\" aria-expanded=\"false\">\n                    <span class=\"faq_question_text\">Does Ren copy famous anime shows?</span>\n                    <svg class=\"faq_chevron\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n                        <path d=\"M6 9L12 15L18 9\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/>\n                    </svg>\n                </button>\n                <div class=\"faq_answer\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-collapsed>\n                    <div class=\"faq_answer_content\"><p>No. Ren designs an original look based on the mood or genre you request, without reproducing any well-known series or its characters.</p>\n</div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"faq_divider\"></div>\n            </div>\n            </div>\n</section>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n    \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n    \"mainEntity\": [\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"What is Ren on Picsart?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"Ren is an AI anime maker built as an agent on Picsart. It makes original anime clips, episodes and series from your ideas, photos or footage.\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"What can you bring to Ren?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"A story idea, a photo or a video clip. Each one leads to a different kind of result, from a new story to an anime version of yourself to restyled footage.\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"How long are Ren's social clips?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"Social clips run from 5 to 30 seconds, in vertical format for TikTok, Reels and Shorts.\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"Can you turn a photo of yourself into an anime character?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"Yes. Ren turns the photo into a character sheet first, then into a moving shot that keeps your likeness.\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"How do characters stay consistent across episodes?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"Each character gets a full turnaround sheet. Once locked, faces, hair and outfits hold in every later shot and episode.\"\n            }\n        },\n        {\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\n            \"name\": \"Does Ren copy famous anime shows?\",\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                \"text\": \"No. Ren designs an original look based on the mood or genre you request, without reproducing any well-known series or its characters.\"\n            }\n        }\n    ]\n}</script>\n\n<script>\n(function() {\n    var container = document.getElementById('faq-faq-6ae3567ec3c5a');\n    if (!container) return;\n\n    var items = container.querySelectorAll('.faq_item');\n    items.forEach(function(item) {\n        var button = item.querySelector('.faq_question');\n        var answer = item.querySelector('.faq_answer');\n        if (!button || !answer) return;\n\n        button.addEventListener('click', function() {\n            var isActive = item.classList.contains('faq_item--active');\n\n            if (isActive) {\n                item.classList.remove('faq_item--active');\n                button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n                answer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n                answer.setAttribute('data-collapsed', '');\n            } else {\n                items.forEach(function(other) {\n                    var otherBtn = other.querySelector('.faq_question');\n                    var otherAnswer = other.querySelector('.faq_answer');\n                    other.classList.remove('faq_item--active');\n                    if (otherBtn) otherBtn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');\n                    if (otherAnswer) {\n                        otherAnswer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n                        otherAnswer.setAttribute('data-collapsed', '');\n                    }\n                });\n                item.classList.add('faq_item--active');\n                button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');\n                answer.removeAttribute('data-collapsed');\n                answer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');\n            }\n        });\n    });\n})();\n</script>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Start_your_first_anime_with_Ren\">Start your first anime with Ren</span></h2>\n<p>Ren is live on Picsart now. Take a story idea, a photo or a video clip to <a href=\"https://picsart.com/ai-agents/ren-anime-studio/\">Ren, the AI anime maker</a> and let it handle the cast, the shots and the edit.</p>\n",
